 ## Background
-Originated from the integration of neural implicit fields with inverse volume rendering. VolSDF [10715-volsdf.md] was one of the early works to explicitly model the SDF for volume rendering, aiming to overcome the ambiguity of density-based representations. NeuS [6060-neus.md] and Surface NeRF [7385-surface-nerf.md] further refined this by introducing specific architectures and optimization strategies (such as hierarchical sampling and alternating optimization) to stabilize training and improve geometric fidelity. Instant-NSR [12440-instant-nsr.md] later adapted the approach for hash-grid acceleration. These methods are primarily used in multi-view stereo reconstruction, 3D asset creation, and augmented reality applications where accurate geometry is as important as photorealistic appearance [6060-neus.md, 7385-surface-nerf.md, 10715-volsdf.md, 12440-instant-nsr.md].
